<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dál Riata</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 500–c. 850</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Dalriada</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dál Riata was a Gaelic kingdom that spanned the western seaboard of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a>, centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argyll">Argyll</a>, and part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-antrim">County Antrim</a> in Ireland, from about the sixth to the ninth century. Its kings ruled from strongholds such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dunadd">Dunadd</a>, and the monastery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iona">Iona</a>, founded by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/columba">Columba</a> within its territory, spread <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. Dál Riata fought and later merged with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picts">Picts</a>, a union from which the kingdom of Alba emerged in the ninth century.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dal-riata.jpg" alt="Dál Riata" width="320" height="453" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Dalriada.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
